pass:
Hello Velin, I have noted that the dining table comes apart and that you will pack the kitchen yourself. Please keep the screws with the table in a labelled bag so they do not disappear into a general box.

For the last evening, it helps to keep one small box out for the kettle, mugs, chargers and anything you will need straight away. Label that box clearly and ask the crew to put it on last. Please empty and dry the washing machine before we arrive. We can carry it, but the appliance connections should already be disconnected.

On the day:
- leave a clear path from each room to the front door;
- point out anything that must stay in the property;
- tell the crew which boxes contain fragile items;
- check cupboards and high shelves before we leave.

You don't need to dismantle the bed if you would like the crew to do it. Just leave the mattress clear. We will check the room labels with you at the new place before unloading.

Best wishes,
Orsa
